# Line ends: git's own guess for text, but bash scripts keep LF in every checkout (bash reads a CR at a line's end as
# part of the command), and images, the GIF, the HDR environment maps and glTF's binary files (a .glb model, a .bin
# buffer beside a .gltf) are binary: never converted, never diffed. A .gltf (glTF's JSON) is kept byte for byte as
# published, its line ends never converted (it still diffs as text), so the SHA-256 pins of the committed models hold
# in every checkout, whatever its core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.hdr binary
*.glb binary
*.bin binary
*.gltf -text
